  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39649010",
      "title": "Using & Outputting Dynamic Values [Core Concept]",
      "sourceHash": "cea4535440cf93dc541d29f42350107bc83585d4c7bc545489c4153b99802e8f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 3.81,
          "en": "So now that we built our first component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.81,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "before we're going to add more components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 12,
          "en": "I wanna explore how we can actually output dynamic content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12,
          "end": 13.44,
          "en": "in such a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.44,
          "end": 15.75,
          "en": "So in our JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.75,
          "end": 19.53,
          "en": "instead of just outputting static content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.53,
          "end": 21.21,
          "en": "to be precise here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.21,
          "end": 23.19,
          "en": "in this Header component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.19,
          "end": 24.87,
          "en": "I wanna make sure that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.87,
          "end": 29.87,
          "en": "here we're not always saying Fundamental React concepts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.3,
          "end": 31.62,
          "en": "but that instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.62,
          "end": 35.958,
          "en": "we sometimes also output Crucial React concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.958,
          "end": 39.21,
          "en": "or Core React concepts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.21,
          "end": 43.35,
          "en": "so that we switch between these three words.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.35,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "And I wanna switch between these options randomly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 49.8,
          "en": "and that will be an important new feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.8,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "that we add to our code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.75,
          "end": 54.15,
          "en": "Because to achieve this goal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.15,
          "end": 57.54,
          "en": "we need to output content dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.54,
          "end": 59.19,
          "en": "And that's, in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.19,
          "end": 62.37,
          "en": "something you will need to do a lot in React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.37,
          "end": 66.57,
          "en": "and that's why we will learn how to do that in this lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.57,
          "end": 71.46000000000001,
          "en": "Now, for that, attached you'll find a new app JSX file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.46000000000001,
          "end": 75.39,
          "en": "which you can simply use to replace your file with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.39,
          "end": 76.44,
          "en": "And if you do so,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.44,
          "end": 80.07,
          "en": "you'll see that it basically adds this code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.07,
          "end": 82.68299999999999,
          "en": "these five lines of code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.91,
          "end": 87.24,
          "en": "And therefore, alternatively, you can of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.24,
          "end": 89.97,
          "en": "also simply grab those lines of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.97,
          "end": 93.275,
          "en": "and paste them into your app JSX file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.275,
          "end": 96.69,
          "en": "Now here in this code, I set up these words,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.69,
          "end": 100.35,
          "en": "which I wanna use, and I have a function which we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 102.75,
          "en": "to produce a random number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.75,
          "end": 105,
          "en": "So in the end, a function which we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105,
          "end": 107.43,
          "en": "to produce a random index,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.43,
          "end": 109.71000000000001,
          "en": "which we can then use to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.71000000000001,
          "end": 114,
          "en": "to these different possible words on a random basis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114,
          "end": 117.47999999999999,
          "en": "Now, to do that, we can go to the place where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.47999999999999,
          "end": 119.85,
          "en": "the dynamic value will be needed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.85,
          "end": 123.66,
          "en": "and that will be here in this Header component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.66,
          "end": 126.33,
          "en": "Here, instead of always outputting Fundamental,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.33,
          "end": 128.82,
          "en": "I wanna output such a random word.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.82,
          "end": 132.06,
          "en": "And therefore, here in this JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.06,
          "end": 134.82,
          "en": "we now don't want a hard-coded value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.82,
          "end": 137.04,
          "en": "like Fundamental or Core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.04,
          "end": 140.16,
          "en": "but instead we wanna output a dynamic value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.16,
          "end": 145.16,
          "en": "And that can be done in JSX and React by using curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.22,
          "end": 151.22,
          "en": "a single pair of curly braces opening and closing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.68,
          "end": 156.68,
          "en": "And when you add curly braces like this in your JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.69,
          "end": 160.11,
          "en": "either like this here between element tags",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.11,
          "end": 164.253,
          "en": "or possibly also as a value for an attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 167.7,
          "en": "you tell JSX and React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.7,
          "end": 171.09,
          "en": "that you wanna output a dynamic value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.09,
          "end": 172.23,
          "en": "To be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.23,
          "end": 176.34,
          "en": "you can now add any JavaScript expression of your choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.34,
          "end": 178.62,
          "en": "between those curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.62,
          "end": 181.62,
          "en": "So, any JavaScript expression code you put",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.62,
          "end": 185.31,
          "en": "between those curly braces will be executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.31,
          "end": 189.24,
          "en": "and it will then be the value of that expression.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 189.24,
          "end": 192.694,
          "en": "So, the result of that calculation here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 192.694,
          "end": 195.63,
          "en": "that will be output on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.63,
          "end": 200.28,
          "en": "So if I do add one plus one between those curly braces here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.28,
          "end": 203.25,
          "en": "we therefore see two on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 203.25,
          "end": 205.14,
          "en": "That's how this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.14,
          "end": 207.93,
          "en": "And therefore, this curly brace syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.93,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "is of course super important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 212.19,
          "en": "because it is the syntax that does allow us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.19,
          "end": 217.19,
          "en": "to blend our hard-coded content with dynamic values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 218.28,
          "end": 222.72,
          "en": "Therefore, here we could reach out to reactDescriptions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.72,
          "end": 225.09,
          "en": "so to this array here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.09,
          "end": 228.603,
          "en": "which is stored in this reactDescriptions constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.47,
          "end": 232.29,
          "en": "and then access an element by index.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.29,
          "end": 234.84,
          "en": "And that index will now be produced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.84,
          "end": 237.27,
          "en": "with the help of that getRandomInt function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.27,
          "end": 238.59300000000002,
          "en": "which I'm executing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.67000000000002,
          "end": 241.71,
          "en": "This function takes one argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.71,
          "end": 244.8,
          "en": "the maximum value I wanna produce.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 244.8,
          "end": 246.63,
          "en": "So here in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.63,
          "end": 249.63,
          "en": "since I have an index with three values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.63,
          "end": 253.29,
          "en": "my maximum number I wanna produce is two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.29,
          "end": 256.983,
          "en": "because the last element has an index of two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 258,
          "end": 259.92,
          "en": "So, therefore, here I pass two",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 259.92,
          "end": 263.13,
          "en": "as a argument to getRandomInt,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 263.13,
          "end": 267.72,
          "en": "and it should be genRandomInt, of course, not getRandomInt,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 267.72,
          "end": 270.543,
          "en": "because genRandomInt is the function name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 271.44,
          "end": 274.32,
          "en": "And if you then save this, you should see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.32,
          "end": 278.04,
          "en": "that you either have Fundamental or Crucial",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.04,
          "end": 283.04,
          "en": "or also Core as a word in front of React concepts here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 283.83,
          "end": 288.33,
          "en": "So now, this is regenerated every time you reload the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 288.33,
          "end": 290.88,
          "en": "since that's the point in time where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 290.88,
          "end": 294.63,
          "en": "this Header component is created and rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 294.63,
          "end": 297.06,
          "en": "and where this Header component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.06,
          "end": 299.55,
          "en": "is therefore executed by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 299.55,
          "end": 302.25,
          "en": "and that's therefore also the point in time where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 302.25,
          "end": 304.593,
          "en": "this code here is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 305.846,
          "end": 307.68,
          "en": "You can, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.68,
          "end": 312.15,
          "en": "also now pull that code out of your JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 312.15,
          "end": 315.003,
          "en": "and store it in a variable or constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 316.62,
          "end": 319.473,
          "en": "which could be named description like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 320.4,
          "end": 324.78,
          "en": "and then just refer to that variable or constant like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 324.78,
          "end": 328.53,
          "en": "This would keep your JSX code a bit leaner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 328.53,
          "end": 332.52,
          "en": "and move that JavaScript expression out of that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 332.52,
          "end": 336.57,
          "en": "which typically is considered a good practice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 336.57,
          "end": 339.18,
          "en": "Even though the code before also worked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 339.18,
          "end": 342.6,
          "en": "keeping your JSX code lean is typically preferred,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 342.6,
          "end": 345.87,
          "en": "and therefore you might wanna go for this option where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 345.87,
          "end": 348.24,
          "en": "you then only refer to the constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 348.24,
          "end": 351.39300000000003,
          "en": "which stores the result of this expression here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 352.23,
          "end": 354.145,
          "en": "Either way, the code works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 354.145,
          "end": 357.39,
          "en": "and we can now switch between these different words",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 357.39,
          "end": 359.043,
          "en": "by reloading the page.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
